# LFX V2 Backend PR Title Convention

When opening a pull request for any LFX V2 / LFX Self-Service backend service repo (e.g. `lfx-v2-*`), the PR title must follow this format:

```
<type>(<scope>): <summary> [<ticket>]
```

**Types:** `feat` | `fix` | `refactor` | `docs` | `chore`

**Examples:**
```
feat(auth): add login button validation [LFXV2-1000]
fix(committee): resolve nil pointer on empty member list [LFXV2-2345]
refactor(project): extract NATS publisher into shared module [LFXV2-3012]
chore(deps): bump Go to 1.22 [LFXV2-4001]
docs(api): update OpenAPI spec for voting endpoints [LFXV2-5678]
```

**Rules:**
- Scope is optional but recommended when the change is isolated to a domain or package.
- Ticket reference is required — always include the Jira issue ID in `[LFXV2-XXXX]` brackets at the end.
- Summary is lowercase, imperative mood, no trailing period.
